  "notes": "Full recipe recovered from the primary literature: base medium 'Mineral salts medium (MSM), Hartmans / de Bont ('HdB') mineral medium, here used 4-fold phosphate-buffered with 1,6-hexamethylenediamine (HMDA) as sole carbon source; host Pseudomonas putida KT2440' (Paper (Nat. Microbiol. 2025, doi:10.1038/s41564-025-01929-5, PMID 39929973) cites its MSM to ref 57 = Wierckx et al. 'Engineering of solvent-tolerant Pseudomonas putida S12 for bioproduction of phenol from glucose', Appl. Environ. Micro",
  "verification": "paper-verified (complete recipe; cited + supplementary sources chased)",
  "verification_evidence": "P. putida KT2440 strains were cultivated in 4-fold buffered (15.52 g l-1 K2HPO4 and 6.52 g l-1 NaH2PO4) MSM medium57.",
  "verification_confidence": "medium",
  "recipe_evidence": "PMC11879879 Methods: 'P. putida KT2440 strains were cultivated in 4-fold buffered (15.52 g l-1 K2HPO4 and 6.52 g l-1 NaH2PO4) MSM medium[57]. Precultures in 2-fold buffered MSM containing 20 mM glucose ... at 30 degC and 180 r.p.m. shaking speed.' and 'HMDA, Ahx, Ahx2, Ahx3 and epsilon-caprolactam ... were used in concentrations of 15 mM as pure substrates.' The base composition beyond the phosphate buffer is not restated in the paper; recovered from the de Bont-group Hartmans/HdB mineral medium: '(NH4)2SO4 2 g L-1, MgCl2.6H2O 0.1 g L-1, ... 10 mL L-1 trace element solution (100 mg L-1 EDTA, 2",
  "recipe_confidence": "medium",
  "base_medium": "Mineral salts medium (MSM), 4-fold phosphate-buffered, = Hartmans-de Bont (HdB) mineral medium as used by the de Bont/Wierckx group; host Pseudomonas putida KT2440. Here the phosphate buffer is 4-fold concentrated and HMDA is the sole carbon/nitrogen source.",
  "base_medium_reference": "Paper (Nat. Microbiol. 2025, doi:10.1038/s41564-025-01929-5, PMID 39929973) cites its MSM to ref 57 = Wierckx et al. 'Engineering of solvent-tolerant Pseudomonas putida S12 for bioproduction of phenol from glucose', Appl. Environ. Microbiol. 71:8221-8227 (2005), doi:10.1128/AEM.71.12.8221-8227.2005, PMID 16332806, PMC1317433. Wierckx 2005 in turn defines MSM ('37 mM phosphate buffer, pH 7.0') per Hartmans et al., Appl. Environ. Microbiol. 55:2850-2855 (1989), doi:10.1128/aem.55.11.2850-2855.1989, PMID 16348047, PMC203180. The full de Bont-group MSM base composition (N source, Mg, trace-element solution) corresponds to the Hartmans-de Bont (HdB) mineral medium, Hartmans, Kaptein, Tramper & de Bont, Appl. Microbiol. Biotechnol. 37:796-801 (1992), doi:10.1007/BF00174849.",
