   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "MSM = de Bont/Wierckx-group Hartmans-de Bont mineral medium; paper only spells out the 4-fold phosphate buffer (15.52 g/L K2HPO4 + 6.52 g/L NaH2PO4) and 15 mM HMDA, and cites ref 57 (Wierckx 2005) for the rest. Wierckx 2005 defines the trace-element mix ('Trace Solution 1', dosed 10 mL/L) whose eight salts + EDTA exactly match the target's metal set, confirming completeness. The base MSM per Wierckx defers to Hartmans (37 mM phosphate, pH 7.0), whose (NH4)2SO4 (2 g/L, 15.1 mM) and MgCl2.6H2O (0.1 g/L, 0.49 mM) primary amounts could not be verbatim-fetched (paywalled Springer / no OA full text)"
  },
